IMPORT prelude

-- Secondhand Goods Dealers Act 2007 (Singapore) -- what counts as secondhand goods (s 2, Schedule), who is deemed a dealer (s 2(2),
-- (3)), the licence requirement and its exemption (ss 4, 20), appeals and when a revocation or suspension bites (ss 5(5), 8, 9),
-- records (s 10), reporting goods matching a police list (s 11), the court's powers when stolen goods were sold to a dealer
-- (s 14), and penalties, employee liability and composition (ss 16, 18, 19).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation "version in force from 9/3/2025", as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/SGDA2007.txt. The revised edition incorporates amendments up to 1 December 2021; the latest
-- amendment annotated in the text is Act 5 of 2025 (wef 9 March 2025, ss 2 and 3); Schedule item 11 is marked deleted by
-- S 519/2023 (wef 31 July 2023). The arrangement of sections at the top of the deposit is numbered one out of step with the
-- body; this encoding follows the body.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance: anyone who sells a used phone, laptop, watch or piece of gold jewellery to
-- a shop, or has one stolen, meets this Act. Not encoded: appointment of the Licensing Officer (s 3), the application form and
-- licence conditions beyond their effect (ss 5(1)-(4), (6), 6), transfer of licences (s 7), the police entry, search and arrest
-- powers (ss 12, 13) beyond a mention, bodies corporate (s 15), court jurisdiction (s 17), and the Minister's rule- and
-- Schedule-amending powers (ss 21, 22). No rules made under s 22 (fees, prescribed record particulars, compoundable offences)
-- were retrieved.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Secondhand Goods Dealers Act 2007 -- dealers`

§§ `2(1) and Schedule -- what counts as secondhand goods`

-- s 2(1): "goods" in "secondhand goods" "means any of the goods specified in the Schedule".
-- Schedule: 1 cameras and photographic equipment; 2 computers, tablets, laptops; 3 handphones and smartphones; 4 CD and MP3/MP4
-- players; 5 "Jewellery set with precious stones"; 6 "Jewellery made from platinum, gold and white gold without precious stones";
-- 7 pawn tickets; 8 watches; 9 copper cables and wires; 10 copper, stainless steel, aluminium, steel or brass items used as
-- fittings of a building, road or other place -- drain covers, manhole covers, railings, water taps and so on; 11 deleted.
--
-- Anything not listed is outside the Act however second-hand it is: clothes, furniture, books, bicycles, televisions. Silver
-- jewellery without precious stones is not in item 6. A bicycle is not listed; a bicycle RACK is (item 10(a)).
DECLARE Item IS ONE OF
    `a used smartphone`
    `a used laptop`
    `a used camera lens`
    `a used MP3 player`
    `a diamond ring`
    `a silver ring set with a sapphire`
    `a plain gold chain`
    `a plain silver bracelet`
    `a pawn ticket`
    `a used watch`
    `a coil of copper cable`
    `a manhole cover`
    `a brass water tap`
    `a used bicycle`
    `a used television`
    `used clothing`
    `used furniture`
    `a used book`

GIVEN `the item` IS AN Item
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the item is secondhand goods under the Act` IF
    CONSIDER `the item`
    WHEN `a plain silver bracelet` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a used bicycle` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a used television` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `used clothing` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `used furniture` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a used book` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `2(2), (3) -- who deals in secondhand goods`

-- s 2(2): dealing "includes a reference to a person in Singapore who deals in secondhand goods through the Internet".
-- s 2(3): every person "in whose shop secondhand goods are found apparently exposed for sale, or who is found in possession of
-- secondhand goods of an unusual quantity, is deemed, until the contrary is proved, to be a person who deals in secondhand goods".
-- "shop" includes a stall, house, flat, storage place or office "whether electronically or otherwise".
-- The Act does not define "deal". Whether a private person selling their own old phone "deals" is not answered by the text; this
-- encoding takes it as a fact.
GIVEN `deals in fact` IS A BOOLEAN, `goods apparently exposed for sale in the person's shop` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `possesses an unusual quantity of secondhand goods` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is treated as a secondhand goods dealer` IF
        `deals in fact`
    OR  (    (`goods apparently exposed for sale in the person's shop` OR `possesses an unusual quantity of secondhand goods`)
         AND (NOT `proved the contrary`))

§§ `4, 20 -- dealing without a licence`

-- s 4(1): "A person must not deal in secondhand goods except under and in accordance with the conditions of a licence issued
-- under section 5." (2) contravention is an offence.
-- s 20(1): the Minister may by Gazette order exempt any person or class; (2) a conditional exemption "operates only if the
-- conditions are complied with".
GIVEN `deals in secondhand goods` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds a licence` IS A BOOLEAN, `complies with the licence conditions` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is exempted by Gazette order` IS A BOOLEAN, `exemption is conditional` IS A BOOLEAN, `complies with exemption conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dealing is an offence under section 4` IF
        `deals in secondhand goods`
    AND (NOT (`holds a licence` AND `complies with the licence conditions`))
    AND (NOT (`is exempted by Gazette order` AND ((NOT `exemption is conditional`) OR `complies with exemption conditions`)))

§§ `5(5), 8(4) -- appeals to the Minister`

-- s 5(5): a person aggrieved by a licensing decision may "within 14 days of being notified of the decision, appeal in writing to
-- the Minister whose decision is final".
-- s 8(4): against a revocation or suspension, within 14 days of receipt of the notice "or such extended period of time as the
-- Minister may allow".
GIVEN `days since notified` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a licensing appeal is in time` IF `days since notified` <= 14

GIVEN `days since notice received` IS A NUMBER, `days allowed by Minister's extension` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a revocation appeal is in time` IF
        `days since notice received` <= 14
    OR  `days since notice received` <= `days allowed by Minister's extension`

§§ `8(1) -- grounds to revoke or suspend`

-- s 8(1)(a): the Licensing Officer satisfied that the licensee (i) has ceased business or, a company, is wound up; (ii) improperly
-- obtained the licence; (iii) is no longer fit and proper; (iv) has been convicted "of any offence involving dishonesty" (or, a
-- company, a managerial or executive officer has); (v) has carried on business so as to be unfit; (vi) failed to comply with a
-- condition; (vii) has contravened any provision of the Act; (viii) has been convicted of an offence under the Act; or (b) "if
-- the Licensing Officer considers it in the public interest to do so".
DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF
    `ceased business or wound up`
    `licence improperly obtained`
    `no longer fit and proper`
    `convicted of an offence involving dishonesty`
    `unfit manner of business`
    `breach of a licence condition`
    `contravened the Act`
    `convicted under the Act`
    `public interest`
    `a customer complaint about prices`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ground permits revocation or suspension` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `a customer complaint about prices` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `8(2), (5), 9 -- when a revocation or suspension takes effect`

-- s 8(2): before revoking or suspending, written notice "specifying a date, not less than 14 days after the date of the notice"
-- and calling on the licensee to show cause.
-- s 8(5): a revocation or suspension "does not take effect until the expiration of a period of 14 days after the Licensing
-- Officer has informed the licensee", and if within that period the licensee gives notice of an appeal, it does not take effect
-- "unless the revocation or suspension order is confirmed by the Minister or the appeal is for any reason dismissed".
-- s 9(1): once effective, "the licensee must cease to carry on the business".
GIVEN `days between show-cause notice and stated date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the show-cause notice gives enough time` IF `days between show-cause notice and stated date` >= 14

GIVEN `days since licensee informed` IS A NUMBER, `appeal notified within 14 days` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `Minister confirmed or dismissed the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the revocation or suspension has taken effect` IF
        `days since licensee informed` > 14
    AND ((NOT `appeal notified within 14 days`) OR `Minister confirmed or dismissed the appeal`)

GIVEN `days since licensee informed` IS A NUMBER, `appeal notified within 14 days` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `Minister confirmed or dismissed the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the licensee must cease business` IF
    `the revocation or suspension has taken effect` `days since licensee informed` `appeal notified within 14 days` `Minister confirmed or dismissed the appeal`

§§ `10 -- records`

-- s 10(1): keep in the shop records of all goods bought (dates, names and addresses of sellers) and sold (dates, names and
-- addresses of buyers); (2) submit them to the Licensing Officer as required; (3) retain them "for a period of not less than 5
-- years from the end of the financial year in which the transactions ... are completed"; (4) produce them on demand to a
-- Magistrate, Justice of the Peace, the Licensing Officer or a police officer.
-- s 10(5): an offence to contravene "subsection (2), (3) or (4)", or to fabricate or produce a record known to be false or
-- misleading. Subsection (1) -- the duty to keep the records at all -- is NOT in the list.
GIVEN `whole years since end of the financial year of the transaction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the record may be discarded` IF `whole years since end of the financial year of the transaction` >= 5

DECLARE RecordFailure IS ONE OF
    `did not keep records in the shop`
    `did not submit records when required`
    `discarded records too early`
    `refused to produce records to police`
    `produced a record known to be false`

GIVEN `the failure` IS A RecordFailure
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the record failure is an offence under section 10(5)` IF
    CONSIDER `the failure`
    WHEN `did not keep records in the shop` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `11 -- goods matching a police list of stolen or lost property`

-- s 11(1): police may circulate lists and descriptions of stolen or lost property to all dealers.
-- (2): if a dealer possesses property fitting the lists, or it is afterwards offered or shown to the dealer, the dealer "(a) must,
-- without unnecessary delay, make a report to any police officer, with the name and address of the person in whose possession the
-- property was seen; and (b) may detain the person offering or showing" it until police arrive.
-- (3): only contravening (2)(a) is an offence. Detaining is a power, not a duty.
GIVEN `property fits a circulated police list` IS A BOOLEAN, `dealer possesses or was offered or shown it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `reported to police without unnecessary delay` IS A BOOLEAN, `detained the person offering it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dealer commits an offence under section 11` IF
        `property fits a circulated police list`
    AND `dealer possesses or was offered or shown it`
    AND (NOT `reported to police without unnecessary delay`)

§§ `14 -- stolen property sold to a dealer`

-- s 14(1): if a person is convicted of an offence under Chapter 17 of the Penal Code 1871 in respect of property sold to a dealer,
-- the court may on proof of ownership order delivery to the owner "either on payment to the secondhand goods dealer of the amount
-- of the purchase price or any part thereof, or without payment", as just according to the owner's conduct.
-- (3): if the dealer "(a) ought reasonably to have known or suspected that the property was stolen property; and (b) did not
-- exercise due care and diligence", the court may order the dealer to pay "a financial penalty not exceeding $2,000".
GIVEN `someone convicted under Penal Code Chapter 17 for the property` IS A BOOLEAN, `property was sold to a dealer` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `ownership proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may order delivery to the owner` IF
    `someone convicted under Penal Code Chapter 17 for the property` AND `property was sold to a dealer` AND `ownership proved`

GIVEN `dealer ought reasonably to have suspected theft` IS A BOOLEAN, `dealer exercised due care and diligence` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `penalty amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the court may order the dealer to pay the penalty` IF
        `dealer ought reasonably to have suspected theft`
    AND (NOT `dealer exercised due care and diligence`)
    AND `penalty amount` <= 2000

§§ `16(2), 18, 19 -- employees, penalties, composition`

-- s 16(2): an agent or employee of a dealer who "wilfully does any act or commits any omission that constitutes an offence" is
-- also guilty, as if carrying on the business.
-- s 18: "a fine not exceeding $20,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or to both".
-- s 19(1): the Licensing Officer may compound an offence "that is prescribed as a compoundable offence" for "a sum not exceeding
-- $2,000"; (2) on payment, no further proceedings.
GIVEN `is an agent or employee of the dealer` IS A BOOLEAN, `acted in the course of the business` IS A BOOLEAN, `acted wilfully` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employee is also guilty` IF
    `is an agent or employee of the dealer` AND `acted in the course of the business` AND `acted wilfully`

GIVEN `fine` IS A NUMBER, `months of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sentence is within the general penalty` IF
    `fine` <= 20000 AND `months of imprisonment` <= 12

GIVEN `offence is prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN, `sum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the offence may be compounded for the sum` IF
    `offence is prescribed as compoundable` AND `sum` <= 2000
